{%- doc -%}
This component is used to show the product gallery (used in product page and featured product section)

@param {object} [product] - the product to render (if empty, renders placeholder content)
@param {string} [product_form_id] - the product form id
@param {string} [desktop_layout] - the layout on desktop (can be "grid", "grid_half", "grid_half_highlight_first" or "carousel")
@param {string} [desktop_carousel_controls] - when desktop layout is set to "carousel", the controls to show (can be "dots", "lines", "numbers", "thumbnails_under", "thumbnails_over", "thumbnails_left" or "bar")
@param {string} [mobile_controls] - the controls to show on mobile (can be "lines", "numbers", "dots", "thumbnails" or "none")
@param {boolean} [enable_media_autoplay] - if set to true videos are autoplayed when switched to
@param {boolean} [enable_video_looping] - if set to true videos automatically loop when finished
@param {boolean} [enable_image_zoom] - if set to true the gallery allow zoom
@param {number} [max_image_zoom_level] - the maximum zoom level allowed (if enabled)
@param {number} [gallery_border_radius] - if set, rounds the bottom corners of the image carousel on mobile
@param {number} [thumbnail_border_radius] - if set, rounds the corners of the gallery thumbnails
@param {string} [class] - extra class applied on the container
@param {boolean} [skip_first_media] - if set to true, product.media's first item is left out of the gallery entirely (used when it's already shown elsewhere, eg. main-product.liquid's separate first-image card)
@param {object} [section]
{%- enddoc -%}

<style>
    @media screen and (max-width: 999px) {
      #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} {
        {%- if mobile_controls == 'none' -%}
          --product-gallery-carousel-grid: auto / auto-flow min(28rem, 75vw);
          --product-gallery-carousel-gap: 0.125rem;
          --product-gallery-carousel-scroll-snap-type: none;
        {%- else -%}
          --product-gallery-gap: {% if mobile_controls != 'thumbnails' %}0rem{% else %}0.5rem{% endif %};
        {%- endif -%}
      }
    }

  {%- comment -%}
  "bar" (bar_controls below - progress bar + page counter + alt-text caption) is selectable both as
  mobile_controls and as desktop_carousel_controls, styled identically either way - only the @media this
  ruleset is wrapped in changes below, so it's captured once here instead of duplicated per breakpoint.

  Normally renders as the image-list's own second grid row, below the carousel. Moved to the top instead,
  using the exact same floating mechanism the other mobile_controls/desktop_carousel_controls variants
  (dots/numbers/thumbnails) already use to sit over the image without adding to the gallery's height -
  .product-gallery__controls-floating's "display: contents" wrapper means this still resolves its
  containing block against .product-gallery__image-list (position: relative, theme.css), same as those.
  Only the anchor edge changes (top here vs. their inset-block-end). The progress-bar element's own
  scroll-tracking (assets/theme.js, track-scroll-target) reads the carousel by id, not DOM position, so it
  keeps working unchanged.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- capture bar_css -%}
    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .product-gallery__controls-floating .product-gallery__top-bar {
      margin-inline: 0;
      padding-inline: var(--container-gutter);
      position: absolute;
      inset-block-start: 1rem;
      inset-inline: 0;
      z-index: 1;
    }

    {%- comment -%}
    The alt-text caption (data-caption per slide, synced by <carousel-caption> in assets/theme.js) sits
    inline with the page-number counter (product-gallery.liquid, both in .product-gallery__caption-row)
    so they share one baseline and font-size, inherited from the body rather than set here. :empty:hidden
    keeps a slide without alt text from leaving a dangling gap after the counter.

    Defaults to the theme's normal text color (assumes a light/studio product photo, the common case).
    .is-dark-image (toggled per slide via data-dark-image + assets/theme.js's updateCaption_fn, same
    event as the caption/counter sync) switches to white with a glow so it stays legible over a dark
    photo - a merchant opts an image into this by adding "!dark" to its alt text in the Shopify admin,
    it's not detected automatically from the pixels.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- comment -%}
    .h-stack (theme.css) defaults align-items to center, which centers the counter against the full
    height of a wrapped 2-line caption - pinning it to flex-start keeps it level with the caption's
    first line regardless of how many lines the alt text wraps to.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .product-gallery__caption-row {
      margin-block-start: .5rem;
      align-items: flex-start;
    }

    {%- comment -%}
    is-dark-image lives on .product-gallery__top-bar (the common ancestor of both the progress bar and
    the caption-row) rather than on the caption-row alone, so .progress-bar picks it up too.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .product-gallery__top-bar {
      color: rgb(var(--text-color));
    }

    {%- comment -%}
    --progress-bar-background-color/--progress-bar-fill-color (css-variables.liquid, from the color
    scheme's progress bar settings) are what .progress-bar (theme.css) actually paints from - they're
    set explicitly there, not left to currentColor's fallback, so color: #fff alone doesn't reach the
    bar. Redefining both variables here overrides them for anything inside this scope instead.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .product-gallery__top-bar.is-dark-image {
      color: #fff;
      --progress-bar-background-color: rgb(255 255 255 / .3);
      --progress-bar-fill-color: #fff;
    }

    {%- comment -%}
    .text-subdued (theme.css, used by the counter's "/" and total-count spans) sets its own
    rgb(var(--text-color) / .6) color rather than inheriting - on a dark image that stays the theme's
    dark text at 60% opacity, nearly invisible against a dark photo, so it needs its own white-based
    override here instead of picking up .is-dark-image's color from above.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .product-gallery__top-bar.is-dark-image .text-subdued {
      color: rgb(255 255 255 / .6);
    }

    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .product-gallery__caption {
      padding-inline-end: .5rem;
      display: block;
    }

    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .product-gallery__caption:empty {
      display: none;
    }
  {%- endcapture -%}

  {%- if mobile_controls == 'bar' -%}
    @media screen and (max-width: 999px) {
      {{ bar_css }}
    }
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- if desktop_carousel_controls == 'bar' -%}
    @media screen and (min-width: 1000px) {
      {{ bar_css }}
    }
  {%- endif -%}

  @media screen and (min-width: 1000px) {
    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} {
      {%- if desktop_layout == 'grid' -%}
        --product-gallery-carousel-grid: auto-flow dense / minmax(0, 1fr);
        --product-gallery-carousel-scroll-snap-type: none;
      {%- elsif desktop_layout == 'grid_half' or desktop_layout == 'grid_half_highlight_first' -%}
        --product-gallery-carousel-grid: auto-flow dense / repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
        --product-gallery-carousel-scroll-snap-type: none;
      {%- elsif desktop_layout == 'carousel' -%}
        --product-gallery-gap: {% if desktop_carousel_controls == 'thumbnails_under' %}0.5rem{% else %}0rem{% endif %};
      {%- endif -%}
    }

    {%- if desktop_layout == 'grid_half_highlight_first' -%}
      #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .product-gallery__media:nth-child(1 of :not([hidden])) {
        grid-column: span 2;
      }
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if desktop_layout == 'carousel' -%}
      {%- comment -%}
      Same inline/block inset as .product-gallery__top-bar (padding-inline: var(--container-gutter),
      inset-block-start: 1rem, both in bar_css above) instead of flush against the edges, mirrored to the
      bottom - reads as one consistent alignment with the bar and with .product-zoom-button below. Bare
      SVGs, no .circle-button background: .product-gallery__nav-button below resets the <button> itself.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .product-gallery__nav-buttons {
        position: absolute;
        inset-inline-start: var(--container-gutter);
        inset-block-end: 1rem;
        align-items: center;
        color: rgb(var(--text-color));
      }

      #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} product-gallery.is-dark-image .product-gallery__nav-buttons {
        color: #fff;
      }

      #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .product-gallery__nav-button {
        background: none;
        border: none;
        padding: .5rem;
        color: inherit;
        cursor: pointer;
        display: grid;
        place-items: center;
      }

      {%- comment -%}
      icon.liquid has no "chevron-left" - flipping chevron-right's own SVG here instead of adding one.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} carousel-prev-button .icon {
        transform: rotate(180deg);
      }
    {%- endif -%}
  }

  {%- comment -%}
  .product-zoom-button (theme.css) inherits currentColor and has a negative inset-inline-end meant to
  slightly overhang a card's edge - here it sits inside the gallery's own overflow: hidden, so that
  negative offset clips it off-center instead. Uses the same inline/block inset as .product-gallery__top-bar
  (padding-inline: var(--container-gutter), inset-block-start: 1rem, bar_css above) mirrored to the bottom
  corner, instead of theme.css's own 8px/-12px offsets, so all three corner controls (bar, nav buttons,
  zoom) share one alignment.

  Defaults to the theme's normal text color and switches to white via .is-dark-image, the same "!dark"
  alt-text tag and <carousel-caption> (assets/theme.js) sync the caption/counter already use - toggled on
  the outer <product-gallery> element (not .product-gallery__top-bar) since the zoom button lives outside
  the bar entirely.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .product-zoom-button {
    color: rgb(var(--text-color));
    inset-inline-end: var(--container-gutter);
    inset-block-end: 1rem;
  }

  #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} product-gallery.is-dark-image .product-zoom-button {
    color: #fff;
  }

  {%- comment -%}
  product-zoom-button__label (theme.css) starts at width: 0, only revealed on
  @media (pointer: fine):hover - on touch devices that hover never fires, so it stays hidden forever.
  Showing it always on mobile instead of on hover here (same fix as media-blocks' carousel).
  {%- endcomment -%}
  @media screen and (pointer: coarse) {
    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .product-zoom-button__label {
      width: auto;
    }
  }

  {%- if gallery_border_radius -%}
    @media screen and (max-width: 999px) {
      #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .product-gallery__carousel-frame {
        border-radius: {{ gallery_border_radius }}px;
        overflow: hidden;
      }

      {%- comment -%}
      The carousel's own .bleed padding-inline reserves peek space for the next/prev slide, which keeps the
      image itself inset from the true edge even though the frame around it reaches full width. Since the
      frame is meant to hug the image exactly, we cancel that peek padding here (margin from .bleed is kept,
      so the carousel still reaches the frame's edge).
      {%- endcomment -%}
      #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .product-gallery__carousel-frame .product-gallery__carousel {
        padding-inline: 0;
        scroll-padding-inline: 0;
      }
    }
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- if thumbnail_border_radius -%}
    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .scroll-marker-group--thumbnails .scroll-marker {
      border-radius: {{ thumbnail_border_radius }}px;
      overflow: hidden;
    }
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- if desktop_carousel_controls == 'thumbnails_left' -%}
    @media screen and (min-width: 1000px) {
      {%- comment -%}
      thumbnails_left is thumbnails_over rotated 90°: same floating mechanism (product-gallery__controls-floating
      is display: contents, so .product-gallery__thumbnail-list and .scroll-marker-group--thumbnails inside it
      are absolutely positioned against .product-gallery__image-list's position: relative, ie. against the
      photo itself), just re-anchored to the left edge and centered vertically instead of centered horizontally
      along the bottom edge.

      .product-gallery__thumbnail-list (theme.css, @media min-width: 700px) is normally pinned bottom
      (inset-block-end: 0, width: 75%, height: 100%) so its flex align-items: flex-end can push the group down
      within it — that alignment step is skipped here since the group positions itself directly (see below), so
      inset-inline-start/inset-block are all this needs to turn it into a full-height strip along the left edge.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .product-gallery__thumbnail-list {
        inset-inline-start: 0;
        inset-block: 0;
        width: auto;
      }

      {%- comment -%}
      --scroll-marker-group-width overrides the 50%/100% used for the horizontal bar (same variable the
      counter variant already uses for its own auto width). left/top/transform re-anchor it from
      "centered along the bottom" to "centered along the left edge"; inset-block-end: auto clears the
      bottom-edge offset the base rule sets, so it doesn't fight with top for the vertical position.
      flex-direction/max-height/overflow turn the horizontal scrolling bar into a vertical one, scrolling
      internally rather than growing past the photo's height when there are many images.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .scroll-marker-group--thumbnails {
        --scroll-marker-group-width: auto;
        left: 1.75rem;
        top: 50%;
        inset-block-end: auto;
        transform: translateY(-50%);
        flex-direction: column;
        max-height: 100%;
        overflow: hidden auto;
      }

      #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .scroll-marker-group--thumbnails .scroll-marker {
        flex-shrink: 0;
      }
    }
  {%- endif -%}
</style>

{%- comment -%}
IMPLEMENTATION NOTE: Shopify does not natively offer a way to create a set of images per variant. This is often
pretty limited when you have a lot of colors and would like to only see the images specific to a given color. To
goes around that, Impact offers a hack using alt tags whose usage is described here: https://support.maestrooo.com/article/187-product-creating-variant-image-set
The implementation is rather complex and inefficient due to a lot of string parsings, but it is, unfortunately, the
only way to do it on Shopify right now.
{%- endcomment -%}
{% liquid
  assign default_media = product.selected_or_first_available_variant.featured_media | default: product.featured_media
  assign product_gallery_carousel_id = 'product-gallery-carousel-' | append: product.id | append: '-' | append: section.id
  assign filtered_indexes = null | sort

  # gallery_media is what every loop below actually renders/counts - product.media itself, unless
  # skip_first_media asks to drop the first item (only when there's more than 1 item to begin with, so
  # the gallery never ends up with zero slides).
  assign gallery_media = product.media
  if skip_first_media and product.media.size > 1
    assign gallery_media = product.media | slice: 1, product.media.size
  endif

  # Rotate gallery_media so default_media (the selected variant's featured media - whichever slide the
  # carousel actually opens on, via .is-initial/ScrollCarousel) becomes its first item, keeping the rest
  # in their original relative order. Without this, the numbers/bar counter and thumbnails order reflect
  # the media's raw catalog position (eg. "2/2" for a variant whose featured image happens to be the
  # product's 2nd photo) instead of viewing order - the photo actually shown first should read "1/N".
  if product != blank and default_media != blank
    assign default_media_position = -1

    for media in gallery_media
      if media == default_media
        assign default_media_position = forloop.index0
        break
      endif
    endfor

    if default_media_position > 0
      assign gallery_media_size = gallery_media.size
      assign rotated_tail_length = gallery_media_size | minus: default_media_position
      assign rotated_tail = gallery_media | slice: default_media_position, rotated_tail_length
      assign rotated_head = gallery_media | slice: 0, default_media_position
      assign gallery_media = rotated_tail | concat: rotated_head
    endif
  endif

  if product.variants.size > 1
    for media in product.media
      # Stripped of the "!dark"/"!light" background-color marker (see caption/counter block below) before
      # splitting on "#" - otherwise a media tagged eg. "Caption#Color_Red!dark" would read "Red!dark" as
      # the option value instead of "Red".
      assign media_alt_clean = media.alt | remove: '!dark' | remove: '!light'

      if media_alt_clean contains '#' and media_alt_clean != product.title
        assign alt_parts = media_alt_clean | split: '#'
        assign media_group_parts = alt_parts.last | split: '_'
        assign option = product.options_by_name[media_group_parts.first]
        assign option_value = option.selected_value | downcase
        assign downcase_group_value = media_group_parts.last | strip | downcase

        if option_value != downcase_group_value and media != default_media
          assign media_position = media.position | sort
          assign filtered_indexes = filtered_indexes | concat: media_position
        endif
      endif
    endfor
  endif

  # Shared by numbers_controls and bar_controls below (both show a "current / total" counter) so the
  # filtered-media counting logic only lives in one place. default_media_caption is the initial value
  # for <carousel-caption> (bar_controls) - same "#"-stripping as each slide's own data-caption below,
  # so the very first paint (before any carousel:change fires) already matches what the JS would set.
  #
  # Uses gallery_media.first rather than default_media directly: when default_media was found above,
  # the rotation already made it gallery_media's first item, so this is the same media. But when
  # skip_first_media has excluded default_media from gallery_media entirely (main-product.liquid's
  # separate first-image card, whose image IS default_media), default_media_position stays -1 and no
  # rotation happens - falling back to gallery_media.first keeps the caption/counter matching whatever
  # slide is actually shown first, instead of describing an image that isn't even in the carousel.
  if product != blank
    assign media_count = gallery_media.size
    assign effective_default_media = gallery_media.first
    assign default_media_index = 0
    assign default_media_caption = effective_default_media.alt | remove: '!dark' | remove: '!light' | split: '#' | first | strip

    # Merchant-controlled background flag: append "!dark" to a media's alt text (in the Shopify admin) to
    # mark it as needing white/glow caption text instead of the default dark-on-light styling - see
    # is-dark-image below and each slide's data-dark-image attribute, kept in sync via <carousel-caption>
    # (assets/theme.js) the same way data-caption already is. No live pixel sampling; this is a manual tag.
    assign default_media_is_dark = false
    if effective_default_media.alt contains '!dark'
      assign default_media_is_dark = true
    endif

    for media in gallery_media
      if filtered_indexes contains media.position
        assign media_count = media_count | minus: 1
      endif
    endfor

    for media in gallery_media
      unless filtered_indexes contains media.position
        assign default_media_index = default_media_index | plus: 1

        if media == effective_default_media
          break
        endif
      endunless
    endfor
  endif
%}

<product-gallery id="product-gallery-{{ product_gallery_carousel_id }}" class="product-gallery {{ class }} {% if product != blank and default_media_is_dark %}is-dark-image{% endif %}" form="{{ product_form_id }}" filtered-indexes="{{ filtered_indexes | json }}" {% if enable_media_autoplay %}autoplay-media{% endif %} {% if enable_image_zoom %}allow-zoom="{{ max_image_zoom_level }}" zoom-color-scheme-id="{{ settings.default_color_scheme.id }}"{% endif %}>
  <div class="product-gallery__image-list">
    {%- comment -%}
    ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    CAROUSEL
    ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    {%- endcomment -%}

    <div class="relative {% if gallery_border_radius %}product-gallery__carousel-frame bleed md:unbleed{% endif %}">
      <scroll-carousel adaptive-height id="{{ product_gallery_carousel_id }}" class="product-gallery__carousel scroll-area bleed md:unbleed" role="region">
        {%- if product != blank -%}
          {%- assign image_index = 0 -%}
          {%- for media in gallery_media -%}
            {%- capture sizes -%}(max-width: 699px) 100vw, 50vw{%- endcapture -%}

            {%- comment -%}
            data-caption: the media's alt text, shown by <carousel-caption> (bar_controls below) below
            the mobile progress bar/counter row, synced to whichever slide is currently in view. Stripped
            of anything from "#" onward, since alt text can also carry the variant-image-set encoding
            described in the IMPLEMENTATION NOTE above (eg. "Some caption#Color_Red") - a real caption
            should never show that raw suffix. Also stripped of "!dark"/"!light" (the background-color
            marker, see default_media_is_dark above) for the same reason - data-dark-image below carries
            that instead, read by the same JS listener to toggle .product-gallery__caption-row's contrast.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <div class="product-gallery__media snap-center {% if media == effective_default_media %}is-initial{% endif %} {% if enable_image_zoom and section.settings.desktop_media_layout contains 'grid' and media.media_type == 'image' %}relative{% endif %}" data-media-type="{{ media.media_type }}" data-media-id="{{ media.id }}" data-caption="{{ media.alt | remove: '!dark' | remove: '!light' | split: '#' | first | strip | escape }}" {% if media.alt contains '!dark' %}data-dark-image{% endif %} role="group" aria-label="{{ 'general.accessibility.item_nth_of_count' | t: index: forloop.index, count: gallery_media.size }}" {% if filtered_indexes contains media.position %}hidden{% endif %}>
              {%- if effective_default_media == media -%}
                {%- assign preload = true -%}
              {%- else -%}
                {%- assign preload = false -%}
              {%- endif -%}

              {%- comment -%}
              NOTE: for the product gallery, the autoplay does not work in a similar way. It is always false at the product level,
              and the product-gallery component itself will autoplay (if needed)
              {%- endcomment -%}
              {%- render 'media', product: product, media: media, sizes: sizes, preload: preload, controls: true, playsinline: true, muted: enable_media_autoplay, loop: enable_video_looping, group: 'product' -%}

              {%- if enable_image_zoom and section.settings.desktop_media_layout contains 'grid' and media.media_type == 'image' -%}
                <open-lightbox-button aria-controls="{{ product_gallery_carousel_id}}" class="block sm-max:hidden" image-index="{{ image_index }}">
                  <button class="product-zoom-button">
                    {%- render 'icon' with 'zoom-plus', width: 16 -%}
                    <span class="product-zoom-button__label">{{ 'product.gallery.zoom' | t }}</span>
                  </button>
                </open-lightbox-button>

                {%- unless filtered_indexes contains media.position -%}
                  {%- assign image_index = image_index | plus: 1 -%}
                {%- endunless -%}
              {%- endif -%}
            </div>
          {%- endfor -%}
        {%- else -%}
          {%- for i in (1..3) -%}
            {%- capture placeholder_name -%}product-apparel-{{ i }}{%- endcapture -%}

            <div class="product-gallery__media snap-center {% if forloop.first %}is-initial{% endif %}" data-media-type="image" role="group" aria-label="{{ 'general.accessibility.item_nth_of_count' | t: index: forloop.index, count: 3 }}">
              {{- placeholder_name | placeholder_svg_tag: 'placeholder' -}}
            </div>
          {%- endfor -%}
        {%- endif -%}
      </scroll-carousel>

      {%- comment -%}
      Replaces the old mouse-following <custom-cursor> click-to-navigate overlay: two static prev/next
      buttons pinned to the bottom-left corner instead. Bare chevron-right SVGs (icon.liquid has no
      chevron-left - carousel-prev-button's is flipped 180deg via CSS above), no button background - only
      for desktop_layout "carousel", since grid layouts show every slide at once and have no single
      "current slide" to step through.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if desktop_layout == 'carousel' and product != blank and gallery_media.size > 1 -%}
        <div class="product-gallery__nav-buttons hidden md:flex gap-1">
          <carousel-prev-button aria-controls="{{ product_gallery_carousel_id }}">
            <button type="button" class="product-gallery__nav-button">
              {%- render 'icon' with 'chevron-right', width: 12 -%}
            </button>
          </carousel-prev-button>

          <carousel-next-button aria-controls="{{ product_gallery_carousel_id }}">
            <button type="button" class="product-gallery__nav-button">
              {%- render 'icon' with 'chevron-right', width: 12 -%}
            </button>
          </carousel-next-button>
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if enable_image_zoom -%}
        <open-lightbox-button aria-controls="{{ product_gallery_carousel_id}}" {% if section.settings.desktop_media_layout contains 'grid' %}class="sm:hidden"{% endif %}>
          <button class="product-zoom-button">
            {%- render 'icon' with 'zoom-plus', width: 16 -%}
            <span class="product-zoom-button__label">{{ 'product.gallery.zoom' | t }}</span>
          </button>
        </open-lightbox-button>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    {%- comment -%}
  ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  CONTROLS
  ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  {%- endcomment -%}

    {%- if gallery_media.size > 1 or product == blank -%}
      {%- comment -%}
      IMPLEMENTATION NOTE: we allow merchants to control independently the desktop and mobile controls. To handle that, we
        render each type of controls, and then add the correct one based on the settings
      {%- endcomment -%}

      {%- comment -%}THUMBNAILS{%- endcomment -%}
      {%- capture thumbnails_controls -%}
        <div class="product-gallery__thumbnail-list">
          <carousel-navigation align-selected aria-controls="{{ product_gallery_carousel_id }}" class="scroll-marker-group scroll-marker-group--thumbnails scroll-area bleed md:unbleed">
            {%- if product != blank -%}
              {%- for media in gallery_media -%}
                <button type="button" class="scroll-marker" {% if filtered_indexes contains media.position %}hidden{% endif %} aria-current="{% if media == effective_default_media %}true{% else %}false{% endif %}" aria-label="{{ 'general.accessibility.go_to_item' | t: index: forloop.index | escape }}">
                  {{- media | image_url: width: media.preview_image.width | image_tag: loading: 'lazy', sizes: '56px', widths: '56,112,168', class: 'object-contain' -}}

                  {%- unless media.media_type == 'image' -%}
                    <div class="product-gallery__media-badge">
                      {%- if media.media_type == 'model' -%}
                        {%- render 'icon' with 'media-model-badge', width: 12 -%}
                      {%- else -%}
                        {%- render 'icon' with 'media-video-badge', width: 12 -%}
                      {%- endif -%}
                    </div>
                  {% endunless %}
                </button>
              {%- endfor -%}
            {%- else -%}
              {%- for i in (1..3) -%}
                {%- capture placeholder_name -%}product-apparel-{% cycle '1', '2', '3', '4', '5' %}{%- endcapture -%}

                <button type="button" class="scroll-marker" aria-current="{% if forloop.first %}true{% else %}false{% endif %}" aria-label="{{ 'general.accessibility.go_to_item' | t: index: forloop.index | escape }}">
                  {{- placeholder_name | placeholder_svg_tag: 'block object-contain h-full w-full' -}}
                </button>
              {%- endfor -%}
            {%- endif -%}
          </carousel-navigation>
        </div>
      {%- endcapture -%}

      {%- comment -%}LINES{%- endcomment -%}

      {%- capture lines_controls -%}
        <carousel-navigation class="scroll-marker-group scroll-marker-group--lines align-self-center" aria-controls="{{ product_gallery_carousel_id }}">
          {%- if product != blank -%}
            {%- for media in gallery_media -%}
              <button type="button" class="scroll-marker tap-area tap-area--sm" {% if filtered_indexes contains media.position %}hidden{% endif %} aria-current="{% if media == effective_default_media %}true{% else %}false{% endif %}">
                <span class="sr-only">{{ 'general.accessibility.go_to_item' | t: index: forloop.index }}</span>
              </button>
            {%- endfor -%}
          {%- else -%}
            {%- for i in (1..3) -%}
              <button type="button" class="scroll-marker tap-area tap-area--sm" aria-current="{% if forloop.first %}true{% else %}false{% endif %}">
                <span class="sr-only">{{ 'general.accessibility.go_to_item' | t: index: forloop.index }}</span>
              </button>
            {%- endfor -%}
          {%- endif -%}
        </carousel-navigation>
      {%- endcapture -%}

      {%- comment -%}DOTS{%- endcomment -%}

      {%- capture dots_controls -%}
        <carousel-navigation class="scroll-marker-group scroll-marker-group--dots align-self-center" aria-controls="{{ product_gallery_carousel_id }}">
          {%- if product != blank -%}
            {%- for media in gallery_media -%}
              <button type="button" class="scroll-marker tap-area tap-area--sm" {% if filtered_indexes contains media.position %}hidden{% endif %} aria-current="{% if media == effective_default_media %}true{% else %}false{% endif %}">
                <span class="sr-only">{{ 'general.accessibility.go_to_item' | t: index: forloop.index }}</span>
              </button>
            {%- endfor -%}
          {%- else -%}
            {%- for i in (1..3) -%}
              <button type="button" class="scroll-marker tap-area tap-area--sm" aria-current="{% if forloop.first %}true{% else %}false{% endif %}">
                <span class="sr-only">{{ 'general.accessibility.go_to_item' | t: index: forloop.index }}</span>
              </button>
            {%- endfor -%}
          {%- endif -%}
        </carousel-navigation>
      {%- endcapture -%}

      {%- capture numbers_controls -%}
        <carousel-navigation class="scroll-marker-group scroll-marker-group--counter align-self-center" aria-controls="{{ product_gallery_carousel_id }}">
          {%- if product != blank -%}
            <carousel-prev-button class="tap-area" aria-controls="{{ product_gallery_carousel_id }}">
              <button type="button">
                {%- render 'icon' with 'arrow-left', width: 9, direction_aware: true -%}
              </button>
            </carousel-prev-button>

            <carousel-page-indicator class="h-stack gap-2" aria-controls="{{ product_gallery_carousel_id }}">
              <span current-slide-index>{{ default_media_index }}</span>
              <span class="text-subdued">/</span>
              <span page-size class="text-subdued">{{ media_count }}</span>
            </carousel-page-indicator>

            <carousel-next-button type="button" class="tap-area" aria-controls="{{ product_gallery_carousel_id }}">
              <button type="button">
                {%- render 'icon' with 'arrow-right', width: 9, direction_aware: true -%}
              </button>
            </carousel-next-button>
          {%- else -%}
            <div class="h-stack gap-3">
              <span current-slide-index>1</span>
              <span class="text-subdued">/</span>
              <span page-size class="text-subdued">3</span>
            </div>
          {%- endif -%}
        </carousel-navigation>
      {%- endcapture -%}

      {%- comment -%}BAR{%- endcomment -%}

      {%- capture bar_controls -%}
        <div class="product-gallery__top-bar full-bleed md:unbleed {% if product != blank and default_media_is_dark %}is-dark-image{% endif %}" style="width: 100%;">
          <progress-bar track-scroll-target="{{ product_gallery_carousel_id }}" class="progress-bar"></progress-bar>

          {%- comment -%}
          Numbering sits inline with the alt-text caption (both meta info about the current slide) rather
          than next to the progress bar - default_media_caption/media_count/default_media_index are all
          computed above. The counter's spans carry no font-size of their own, so like the caption they
          just inherit the body's, keeping the two visually paired.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <div class="product-gallery__caption-row h-stack justify-between gap-2 align-self-center">
            {%- comment -%}
            The currently visible slide's alt text (data-caption, set per-slide above), kept in sync via
            <carousel-caption> (assets/theme.js) listening for the same carousel:change event
            carousel-page-indicator already listens to - default_media_caption (computed above) is only
            the FIRST paint's value, before any swipe/click has fired that event yet.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            {%- if product != blank -%}
              <carousel-caption class="product-gallery__caption" aria-controls="{{ product_gallery_carousel_id }}">{{ default_media_caption }}</carousel-caption>
            {%- endif -%}

            <carousel-page-indicator class="h-stack gap-2 shrink-0" aria-controls="{{ product_gallery_carousel_id }}">
              {%- if product != blank -%}
                <span current-slide-index>{{ default_media_index }}</span>
                <span class="text-subdued">/</span>
                <span page-size class="text-subdued">{{ media_count }}</span>
              {%- else -%}
                <span current-slide-index>1</span>
                <span class="text-subdued">/</span>
                <span page-size class="text-subdued">3</span>
              {%- endif -%}
            </carousel-page-indicator>
          </div>
        </div>
      {%- endcapture -%}

      {%- if desktop_layout == 'carousel' -%}
        <div class="{% if desktop_carousel_controls != 'thumbnails_under' %}product-gallery__controls-floating{% endif %} hidden md:contents">
          {%- liquid
            case desktop_carousel_controls
              when 'dots'
                echo dots_controls

              when 'lines'
                echo lines_controls

              when 'thumbnails_under' or 'thumbnails_over' or 'thumbnails_left'
                echo thumbnails_controls

              when 'numbers'
                echo numbers_controls

              when 'bar'
                echo bar_controls
            endcase
          -%}
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if mobile_controls != 'none' -%}
        <div class="{% if mobile_controls != 'thumbnails' %}product-gallery__controls-floating{% endif %} contents md:hidden">
          {%- liquid
            case mobile_controls
              when 'dots'
                echo dots_controls

              when 'lines'
                echo lines_controls

              when 'thumbnails'
                echo thumbnails_controls

              when 'numbers'
                echo numbers_controls

              when 'bar'
                echo bar_controls
            endcase
          -%}
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>

  {%- comment -%}
  ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  VIEW IN YOUR SPACE
  ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- assign first_3d_model = gallery_media | where: 'media_type', 'model' | first -%}

  {%- if first_3d_model -%}
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdn.shopify.com/shopifycloud/model-viewer-ui/assets/v1.0/model-viewer-ui.css" media="print" onload="this.media='all'; this.onload = null">

    <div class="view-in-space-button md:hidden">
      <button class="button w-full" data-shopify-xr data-shopify-model3d-id="{{ first_3d_model.id }}" data-shopify-model3d-default-id="{{ first_3d_model.id }}" data-shopify-title="{{ product.title | escape }}" data-shopify-xr-hidden>
        <span class="text-with-icon justify-center">
          {%- render 'icon' with 'media-view-in-space' -%}
          {{- 'product.general.view_in_space' | t -}}
        </span>
      </button>
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}
</product-gallery>